# Lightdash client

`internal/lightdash/api` is the HTTP client. `models` holds request and response structs plus small pure helpers that map Terraform fields to API fields (space visibility lives in `space_visibility.go`). `services` groups API calls. Keep projection helpers next to the types they map, with unit tests in the same package.

Unit tests under `internal/lightdash` do not call the network and do not mock the HTTP client. They cover enum validation, JSON marshalling, and pure helpers.

New endpoints go through `.claude/skills/implement-verified-lightdash-api-client`. New Terraform resources go through `.claude/skills/implement-terraform-provider-resource`.
